PZMap API — Setup and Usage Guide

This service provides a simple HTTP API around the existing PZMapCreation project.

It does not replace or modify the existing GeoJSON/map-generation code.

The API accepts three GeoJSON files:

    buildings.geojson

    roads.geojson

    area.geojson

    it finds those files in

    curl -X POST \
    http://localhost:8080/api/maps \
    -F "buildings=@$HOME/pzgis/buildings.geojson" \
    -F "roads=@$HOME/pzgis/roads.geojson" \
    -F "area=@$HOME/pzgis/area.geojson" \
    --output PZGisImport.zip


It passes those files to the existing:

java -cp out pzformat.Probe giscells

command and returns the generated PZGisImport Project Zomboid mod as a ZIP file.
1. Required Directory Layout

The existing PZMapCreation repository should remain at:

~/Documents/PZMapCreation

The API project can be placed alongside it:

~/Documents/
├── PZMapCreation/
│   ├── src/
│   ├── out/
│   └── ...
│
└── pz-map-api/
    ├── app.py
    ├── requirements.txt
    └── .venv/

The Project Zomboid installation should be available at:

$PZ

with its media directory at:

$PZ/media

The GIS GeoJSON files can live anywhere, but the recommended location is:

~/pzgis/
├── buildings.geojson
├── roads.geojson
└── area.geojson

The API does not require the files to remain in ~/pzgis/ when making an API request. They are uploaded to the API, which creates temporary copies for the generation process.
2. GeoJSON Files

The API expects three files.
buildings.geojson

Contains the building GIS data.

Recommended location:

~/pzgis/buildings.geojson

roads.geojson

Contains the road GIS data.

Recommended location:

~/pzgis/roads.geojson

area.geojson

Contains the area/boundary information used by the existing GIS generation process.

Recommended location:

~/pzgis/area.geojson

Verify that they exist:

ls -lh ~/pzgis/

You should see:

buildings.geojson
roads.geojson
area.geojson

These are the files that will be uploaded to the API.
3. PZMapCreation

The API uses the existing PZMapCreation repository.

Its location is:

~/Documents/PZMapCreation

The API expects the compiled Java classes to be in:

~/Documents/PZMapCreation/out

If out does not exist, compile PZMapCreation:

cd ~/Documents/PZMapCreation

rm -rf out
mkdir out

javac -d out (find src/main/java -name '*.java')

Verify:

ls out

4. Verify PZMapCreation Directly

Before using the API, it is useful to verify that the underlying map generator works.

From:

~/Documents/PZMapCreation

run:

java -cp out pzformat.Probe giscells \
    ~/pzgis/buildings.geojson \
    ~/pzgis/roads.geojson \
    ~/pzgis/area.geojson \
    "$PZ/media" \
    ~/Zomboid/mods \
    PZGisImport

This is the existing PZMapCreation command.

The API simply runs the equivalent command using temporary uploaded files.

If this command works, the underlying map generation system is working.
5. API Configuration

The API uses environment variables for the locations of PZMapCreation and the Project Zomboid media directory.

Because this setup uses fish shell, configure them with:

set -x PZMAPCREATION "$HOME/Documents/PZMapCreation"
set -x PZ_MEDIA "$PZ/media"

Verify:

echo $PZMAPCREATION
echo $PZ_MEDIA

Expected result:

/home/your-user/Documents/PZMapCreation
/home/your-user/.../ProjectZomboid/projectzomboid/media

The PZ environment variable must already point to your Project Zomboid installation.

Verify it with:

echo $PZ

6. API Python Environment

Go to the API directory:

cd ~/Documents/pz-map-api

Create the Python virtual environment:

python3 -m venv .venv

Activate it in fish:

source .venv/bin/activate.fish

Install the dependencies:

pip install fastapi "uvicorn[standard]" python-multipart

If requirements.txt is being used instead, run:

pip install -r requirements.txt

7. Starting the API

Make sure the environment variables are set:

set -x PZMAPCREATION "$HOME/Documents/PZMapCreation"
set -x PZ_MEDIA "$PZ/media"

Activate the Python environment:

source ~/Documents/pz-map-api/.venv/bin/activate.fish

Start the API:

cd ~/Documents/pz-map-api

uvicorn app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080

The API should report that it is running on:

http://0.0.0.0:8080

Leave this terminal running while using the API.
8. Check API Health

Open another terminal.

Run:

curl http://localhost:8080/health

A successful response should contain:

{
    "status": "ok"
}

The response will also show the configured PZMapCreation and Project Zomboid media paths.

If the health check fails, check:

    PZMAPCREATION

    PZ_MEDIA

    ~/Documents/PZMapCreation/out

    The Project Zomboid installation

9. Generate a Map

The API endpoint is:

POST /api/maps

It accepts three uploaded files:

buildings
roads
area

Using the recommended GeoJSON locations:

curl -X POST \
    http://localhost:8080/api/maps \
    -F "buildings=@$HOME/pzgis/buildings.geojson" \
    -F "roads=@$HOME/pzgis/roads.geojson" \
    -F "area=@$HOME/pzgis/area.geojson" \
    --output PZGisImport.zip

The API will:

    Receive the three GeoJSON files.

    Create a temporary working directory.

    Save the uploaded files there.

    Invoke the existing PZMapCreation giscells command.

    Generate PZGisImport.

    ZIP the generated mod.

    Return the ZIP to the client.

    Remove the temporary working files.

The original GeoJSON files in ~/pzgis/ are not modified.
10. Check the Generated Map

After the API request completes:

ls -lh PZGisImport.zip

Inspect the archive:

unzip -l PZGisImport.zip

The ZIP should contain the generated:

PZGisImport/

mod structure.

You can extract it with:

unzip PZGisImport.zip

11. Complete Start-to-Finish Procedure

For a normal map-generation session:
Terminal 1 — Start API

set -x PZMAPCREATION "$HOME/Documents/PZMapCreation"
set -x PZ_MEDIA "$PZ/media"

cd ~/Documents/pz-map-api
source .venv/bin/activate.fish

uvicorn app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080

Terminal 2 — Verify inputs

ls -lh ~/pzgis/

Confirm:

buildings.geojson
roads.geojson
area.geojson

Terminal 2 — Generate map

curl -X POST \
    http://localhost:8080/api/maps \
    -F "buildings=@$HOME/pzgis/buildings.geojson" \
    -F "roads=@$HOME/pzgis/roads.geojson" \
    -F "area=@$HOME/pzgis/area.geojson" \
    --output PZGisImport.zip

Terminal 2 — Inspect result

unzip -l PZGisImport.zip

The resulting:

PZGisImport.zip

is the generated Project Zomboid map/mod deliverable.
12. How the System Works

The API is deliberately just a wrapper around the existing PZMapCreation functionality.

The complete flow is:

~/pzgis/
    │
    ├── buildings.geojson
    ├── roads.geojson
    └── area.geojson
             │
             │ HTTP upload
             ▼
      ┌─────────────────┐
      │     FastAPI     │
      │     app.py      │
      └────────┬────────┘
               │
               │ temporary files
               ▼
      ┌─────────────────────┐
      │    PZMapCreation    │
      │                     │
      │ pzformat.Probe      │
      │       giscells      │
      └──────────┬──────────┘
                 │
                 │ existing
                 │ map generation
                 ▼
          PZGisImport/
                 │
                 ▼
          PZGisImport.zip
                 │
                 ▼
             API client

The existing PZMapCreation code is responsible for processing the GIS data and creating the Project Zomboid map.

The API is responsible only for:

    accepting files

    creating temporary files/directories

    invoking PZMapCreation

    collecting the generated mod

    returning the ZIP

