14. The Important Command

If you ever need to bypass the API and run PZMapCreation directly, this is the command:

java -cp out pzformat.Probe giscells \
    ~/pzgis/buildings.geojson \
    ~/pzgis/roads.geojson \
    ~/pzgis/area.geojson \
    "$PZ/media" \
    ~/Zomboid/mods \
    PZGisImport

The API does the same thing, except the three GeoJSON paths point to temporary uploaded files and the output goes to a temporary directory.
15. Changing the GeoJSON Files

To generate a different map, replace the files in:

~/pzgis/

with the new:

buildings.geojson
roads.geojson
area.geojson

Then make the same API request:

curl -X POST \
    http://localhost:8080/api/maps \
    -F "buildings=@$HOME/pzgis/buildings.geojson" \
    -F "roads=@$HOME/pzgis/roads.geojson" \
    -F "area=@$HOME/pzgis/area.geojson" \
    --output PZGisImport.zip

The API does not care where the GeoJSON files originally came from. It simply uploads them to the existing giscells processing pipeline.
16. Current Scope

This setup is intended as a simple local API wrapper.

It does not currently provide:

    authentication

    persistent job storage

    a database

    a job queue

    multiple simultaneous generation jobs

    cloud storage

    automatic deployment

    a web UI

Those can be added later if needed.

For the current use case, the entire process is:

Upload 3 GeoJSON files
        ↓
PZMapCreation
        ↓
PZGisImport.zip

The existing PZMapCreation project remains unchanged.
